---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getApp, COMPANY } from '../../data/apps';

const app = getApp('pulsewire')!;
const lastUpdated = 'June 24, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${app.name} Privacy Policy — ${COMPANY.name}`}
  description={`How ${app.name} collects, uses, and protects your information.`}
  path={`/${app.slug}/privacy`}
  noindex={true}
>
  <article class="prose container">
    <a class="back-link" href="/pulsewire">← {app.name}</a>
    <h1>{app.name} Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated} · DRAFT</p>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how {COMPANY.name} (“we”, “us”) handles
      information in connection with the {app.name} application and website
      (the “Service”), an AI-native RSS and news reader. We aim to collect as
      little as possible and to keep what we do collect private and secure.
      <strong>This document is a working draft.</strong>
    </p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Account information.</strong> When you sign in, we use Microsoft
        identity services. We receive a unique account identifier and basic
        profile details such as your name and email address so we can create and
        secure your account.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your reading data.</strong> Content and activity you generate in
        the app — such as the feeds you subscribe to, articles you read or save,
        and the AI-generated executive briefs and signal scores produced for
        those articles — so the Service can assemble your personalized reader.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Limited technical data.</strong> Basic operational logs (such as
        request timestamps and error information) needed to run, secure, and
        troubleshoot the Service.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do <strong>not</strong> collect precise location, contacts, or device
      advertising identifiers, and we do not use third-party advertising or
      cross-app tracking.
    </p>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To provide, maintain, and secure your account and the Service.</li>
      <li>
        To deliver your subscribed feeds and generate AI briefs and signal
        scores for the articles in your reader.
      </li>
      <li>To diagnose problems and improve reliability and performance.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How your information is stored and protected</h2>
    <p>
      Your feed subscriptions, read and saved articles, and AI-generated briefs
      and signal scores are stored in your own per-user private database.
      Information is encrypted in transit using HTTPS, and the Service is hosted
      on Microsoft Azure. Access is limited to what is necessary to operate the
      Service.
    </p>

    <h2>AI processing</h2>
    <p>
      Executive briefs and signal scores are generated by sending article
      content to our AI provider solely to produce summaries and ratings for
      your reader. Your reading activity is not used to train third-party models.
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal information. We share information only with
      infrastructure providers that host and secure the Service (for example,
      Microsoft Azure for hosting and identity, and our AI provider for
      generating briefs), and only as needed to operate it, or where required by
      law.
    </p>

    <h2>Data retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      We retain your information for as long as your account is active. You may
      request access to, or deletion of, your account and associated data by
      emailing
      <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is intended for a general, adult audience and is not directed
      to children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
      children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be
      reflected by updating the “Last updated” date above.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or your data? Email
      <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
